		},
		{
			"id": "legend",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Legend\n🔴 **Red** = To Do (ready)\n⬜ **Gray** = Blocked\n🟠 **Orange** = Doing\n🔵 **Cyan** = Ready to review\n🟢 **Green** = Done\n🟣 **Purple** = Proposed by agent",
			"x": -540,
			"y": -310,
			"width": 380,
			"height": 230,
			"color": "0"
		},
		{
			"id": "canvas-warnings",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Warnings\n✓ None",
			"x": -540,
			"y": -530,
			"width": 380,
			"height": 200,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "17ed4e1d",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## CLU-02 Frequency-based recents\nReplace recent-only sorting in getRecentlyAddedIntake with frequency-based sorting (most-logged first). Most-eaten foods should always be at the top of the list.\n\n### Changes\n- Replaced recency-only sorting in `getRecentlyAddedIntake()` with frequency-based sorting\n- Counts how many times each food item was logged, sorts most-frequent first\n- Recency used as tiebreaker for items with equal frequency\n- Keeps the latest intake DBO for each food (preserving most recent serving info)",
			"x": 570,
			"y": 128,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 252,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "80984d70",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## CLU-03 Remember last-used quantity\nWhen re-logging a food item, pre-fill the quantity field with the last amount used for that specific food. Look up from intake history by meal code/name.\n\n### Changes\n- Added `getLastIntakeForMeal()` to IntakeDataSource â€” finds most recent intake by food code/name\n- Exposed through IntakeRepository â†’ GetIntakeUsecase â†’ MealDetailBloc\n- Added `getLastUsedAmount()` to MealDetailBloc (injected GetIntakeUsecase as 5th param)\n- MealDetailScreen now async-loads last-used quantity in `_setInitialQuantity()`\n- Falls back to default (100g/1 serving) if no prior intake exists\n- Updated locator registration for MealDetailBloc",
			"x": 1060,
			"y": 104,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 300,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "5793d5b1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## CLU-05 Simplified custom meal entry\nReduce required fields for custom meal to just name + kcal. All other fields (macros, brands, serving) optional. For quick 'I ate ~500kcal of pasta' moments.\n\n### Changes\n- Restructured EditMealScreen: name + kcal at top, macros in a compact row below\n- Brands, meal size, serving size, unit selector, base quantity hidden behind 'More details' collapsible\n- Removed confirmation dialog for custom meal creation (direct navigation)\n- Added `additionalInfoLabel` to EN/DE/TR localizations + generated files\n- Layout: essential fields first (name, kcal, macros row), optional details collapsed",
			"x": 1550,
			"y": 116,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 276,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "c12f9595",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## CLU-01 Search debounce\nAdd 300-400ms debounce to meal_search_bar.dart onChanged callback. Prevents firing network requests on every keystroke.\n\n### Changes\n- Added 400ms debounce timer in AddMealScreen\n- Listens to _searchStringListener changes and debounces before dispatching BLoC events\n- Manual search button and onSubmitted still fire immediately\n- Timer properly cancelled on dispose",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 128,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 252,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "caca0315",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## DM-01 Add sodium to nutriments\nAdd nullable sodium_mg field to MealNutrimentsDBO (append-only, won't break existing data). Map it from OFF (sodium_100g) and FDC (nutrient ID 1093). Display in meal detail UI.\n\n### Changes\n- Added `sodiumMg100` (nullable double, HiveField 7) to MealNutrimentsDBO\n- Added `sodiumMg100` to MealNutrimentsEntity with `sodiumMgPerUnit` getter\n- Updated OFF DTO: added `sodium_100g` field, converts gâ†’mg in entity factory\n- Updated FDC: added `fdcTotalSodiumId = 1093` constant, mapped in entity factory\n- Updated all .g.dart files (Hive adapter + JSON serialization)\n- Updated EditMealBloc to preserve sodium on edit",
			"x": 80,
			"y": 1052,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 300,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "4c0eb41c",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## DM-02 Add MealSource.ai enum value\nAdd 'ai' to MealSourceDBO enum so LLM-estimated meals are tagged with their source. Append-only to avoid breaking Hive.\n\n### Changes\n- Added `ai` value to `MealSourceDBO` enum (HiveField 4) and `MealSourceEntity` enum\n- Updated both switch-based factory methods for DBOâ†”Entity conversion\n- Updated `MealSourceDBOAdapter` (read/write) in .g.dart\n- Updated JSON enum map in .g.dart\n- Added `MealSourceEntity.ai` handling to `MealInfoButton` (URL + label)\n- Added `additionalInfoLabelAI` localization in EN/DE/TR",
			"x": 570,
			"y": 1052,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 300,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "6b3d8c01",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## DM-04 Local food overrides database\nNew Hive box for locally saved/corrected food items, keyed by barcode or user-generated ID. When a barcode is scanned, check local overrides first before hitting OFF/FDC. Used by both label extraction and manual correction flows.\n\n### Changes\n- Created `LocalFoodDataSource` at `lib/core/data/data_source/local_food_data_source.dart`\n  - Uses a separate Hive Box<MealDBO> keyed by barcode/custom ID\n  - Methods: saveFood, deleteFood, getFoodByKey, searchByName, getAllLocalFoods\n- Registered LocalFoodBox in HiveDBProvider (encrypted)\n- Registered LocalFoodDataSource in locator\n- Injected into ProductsRepository as 4th parameter\n- `getOFFProductByBarcode()` now checks local overrides FIRST before hitting OFF API\n- Added `saveLocalFoodOverride()` to ProductsRepository for saving corrected items",
			"x": 1550,
			"y": 1028,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 348,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "c9b074ee",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## DM-03 Meal presets model\nNew MealPresetDBO: name + list of (MealDBO reference, default amount, unit). Hive TypeAdapter with new type ID. Repository + data source for CRUD. Allows saving and recalling groups of food items as a single meal.\n\n### Changes\n- Created `MealPresetDBO` (Hive Type ID: 15) with id, name, and items list\n- Created `MealPresetItemDBO` (Hive Type ID: 16) with MealDBO reference, amount, unit\n- Created `MealPresetDataSource` with CRUD operations (add, delete, update, getAll, getById)\n- Registered adapters in HiveDBProvider + opened MealPresetBox\n- Registered MealPresetDataSource in locator\n- Hand-written .g.dart adapter file",
			"x": 1060,
			"y": 1052,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 300,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "7f0c4295",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## IN-02 AI provider abstraction\nCreate AiProvider interface with estimateFromPhoto(image) and extractFromLabel(image). Two implementations: GeminiProvider, OpenAiProvider. Config selects which one. Both return the same AiNutritionDTO (structured JSON with items array, per_100g values, estimated_weight_g, confidence).\n\n### Changes\n- Created `AiProvider` abstract interface at `lib/features/add_meal/data/data_sources/ai/ai_provider.dart`\n- Created `GeminiProvider` implementation using Gemini 2.0 Flash with vision + structured JSON output\n- Created `OpenAiProvider` implementation using GPT-4o-mini with vision + JSON mode\n- Created `AiNutritionResponseDTO` with items array, per_100g values, clarification support\n- Both providers use identical JSON schema for consistent output\n- Added `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `OPENAI_API_KEY` to env.dart\n- Registered `AiProvider` in locator (Gemini primary, OpenAI fallback)\n- Clarification flow built into the DTO: `needsClarification` flag + `AiClarificationRequest`",
			"x": 2530,
			"y": 80,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 348,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "7bd86f44",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## IN-01 Schema versioning & migrations\nAdd schemaVersion to ConfigDBO. Create a MigrationRunner that runs on app startup, checks version, and applies sequential migrations. All future DBO changes go through this system. Ensures logs survive updates.\n\n### Changes\n- Added `schemaVersion` (nullable int, HiveField 9) to ConfigDBO\n- Created MigrationRunner class at `lib/core/utils/migration_runner.dart`\n- Added `setSchemaVersion()` to ConfigDataSource\n- Wired MigrationRunner into locator.dart (runs after config init)\n- Updated .g.dart for Hive adapter + JSON serialization\n- Baseline migration v0â†’v1 is a no-op; future migrations append to the list",
			"x": 5225,
			"y": 104,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 300,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "776ffad8",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## CLU-07 Add meal entry point redesign\nReplace current add meal screen with a 4-option entry point: Camera (AI photo), Gallery (AI photo), Search/Barcode (existing flow), Recent/Presets (frequency-sorted one-tap logging). This becomes the first screen when tapping 'Add to Breakfast/Lunch/etc'. Camera and Gallery feed into the AI estimation pipeline (single item vs meal choice). Search keeps the existing search+barcode flow. Recent shows most-logged items for one-tap re-logging.",
			"x": 4260,
			"y": 2756,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 384,
			"color": "1"
		},
		{
			"id": "4ac458bf",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## AL-01 Unified AI food input (Magic)\n4-option entry point when adding a meal: Magic, Search, Scan, Recent.\n\n**Magic screen:** Camera button, gallery button, text input field â€” use any combo. Before submitting, choose 'Single item' or 'Meal breakdown'. LLM returns structured JSON.\n\n- Single item â†’ 1 entry with combined macros â†’ review/tweak â†’ save\n- Meal breakdown â†’ ingredient list grouped under a meal name (groupId/groupName on IntakeDBO) â†’ review/tweak each â†’ save all. Diary shows meal name collapsed, tap to expand ingredients.\n\nReplaces old custom meal creation. Added groupId (HiveField 6) and groupName (HiveField 7) to IntakeDBO for meal grouping.",
			"x": 3120,
			"y": 1274,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 382,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "63b2f1b3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## CLU-06 Meal presets UI\nUI to create, edit, and quick-log meal presets. One tap to log a full preset (e.g. 'My usual breakfast'). Allow quantity adjustments before confirming.",
			"x": 4260,
			"y": 2120,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "0"
		},
		{
			"id": "5d86317e",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## AL-02 Label photo extraction flow\nTriggered from: (1) unknown barcode scan, or (2) 'correct this item' action on a fetched product. Take photo of nutrition label â†’ send to AiProvider.extractFromLabel â†’ LLM extracts exact values â†’ save to local overrides DB â†’ proceed with logging. LLM may ask follow-up if label is unclear.",
			"x": 3640,
			"y": 1600,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 244,
			"color": "1"
		},
		{
			"id": "d20d9853",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## CLU-04 Quick-log from search results\nSkip the full MealDetailScreen for known items. Tap item in search results â†’ inline quantity picker â†’ confirm. Detail screen accessible via long-press or info icon. Reduces logging from 6-7 taps to 3-4.",
			"x": 4260,
			"y": 1320,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 228,
			"color": "1"
		},
		{
			"id": "186ef498",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## AL-03 LLM clarification dialog\nReusable chat-like widget for LLM follow-up questions. When the LLM response includes a clarification request, show it to the user, collect answer, re-submit. Keeps the flow conversational without breaking the logging UX. Used by both photo estimation and label extraction.\n\n### Changes\nBuilt as part of AL-01 Magic screen. Clarification dialog shows LLM question + suggested answer chips + free text input. Recursive re-submit on answer.",
			"x": 3640,
			"y": 1202,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 228,
			"color": "5"
		}
	],
